# Chat-independent documentation

**Chat transcripts are not the system of record.** Before finishing a substantive turn (code, design decisions, operational steps, investigation conclusions, or verification), the same material must exist in versioned files so deleting chats causes no unique loss.

## What to update (this repo)

| Kind of change | Write it here |
|---|---|
| Product / flow / policy | `specs/PLATFORM_CONTEXT.md` (decision precedence still applies) |
| Data model | `specs/DATABASE-DESIGN.md` and `specs/exhibition_portal_schema.sql` |
| Delivery sequence | `specs/BUILD-PLAN.md` |
| Verification commands | `specs/TESTING.md` |
| Visitor UI behaviour | `frontend/README.md`, `specs/FRONTEND_BUILD_PROMPT.md` if the contract changed, `frontend/src/features/inquiry/copy.ts` for visitor strings |
| Public Windows host | `specs/DEPLOY-WINDOWS.md` |
| Visual system | `.stitch/DESIGN.md` only when the design system itself changed — do not restyle from stale HTML |

A short dated subsection is enough. Do not leave “how to repeat this” only in chat.

## Minimum bar

If the only place a decision, command sequence, verification path, or “what we changed” lives is the chat thread, copy it into the matching file above.

## Scope

- Applies when the turn **changes** something durable (code, config, agreed behaviour, runbook, or non-obvious findings others must reuse).
- Pure Q&A with no project impact does not require new files.
- Does **not** authorize unsolicited doc spam. Pair with **post-change-testing-and-docs**.
- If the user says **`delete this chat`**, also follow **delete-this-chat-handoff**.
